{"path":"std/fs/struct.DirEntry.html","title":"Struct DirEntry","description":"Entries returned by the ReadDir iterator.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"main-content"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Struct DirEntry"}]},{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0 · "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/std/fs.rs.html#235","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"pub struct DirEntry(/* private fields */);"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Entries returned by the "},{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/struct.ReadDir.html","title":"struct std::fs::ReadDir","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"ReadDir"}]},{"type":"text","value":" iterator."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An instance of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"DirEntry"},{"type":"text","value":" represents an entry inside of a directory on the filesystem. Each entry can be inspected via methods to learn about the full path or possibly other metadata through per-platform extension traits."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"platform-specific-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Platform-specific behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On Unix, the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"DirEntry"},{"type":"text","value":" struct contains an internal reference to the open directory. Holding "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"DirEntry"},{"type":"text","value":" objects will consume a file handle even after the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"ReadDir"},{"type":"text","value":" iterator is dropped."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that this "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/index.html#platform-specific-behavior","title":"mod std::io","children":[{"type":"text","value":"may change in the future"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"headin