"type":"heading","level":5,"id":"platform-specific-behavior-1","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Platform-specific behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On Windows this function is cheap to call (no extra system calls needed), but on Unix platforms this function is the equivalent of calling "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"symlink_metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" on the path."}]},{"type":"heading","level":5,"id":"examples-1","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"use std::fs;\n\nif let Ok(entries) = fs::read_dir(\".\") {\n    for entry in entries {\n        if let Ok(entry) = entry {\n            // Here, `entry` is a `DirEntry`.\n            if let Ok(metadata) = entry.metadata() {\n                // Now let's show our entry's permissions!\n                println!(\"{:?}: {:?}\", entry.path(), metadata.permissions());\n            } else {\n                println!(\"Couldn't get metadata for {:?}\", entry.path());\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0Afn+main()+%7B%0A++++use+std::fs;%0A++++%0A++++if+let+Ok(entries)+=+fs::read_dir(%22.%22)+%7B%0A++++++++for+entry+in+entries+%7B%0A++++++++++++if+let+Ok(entry)+=+entry+%7B%0A++++++++++++++++//+Here,+%60entry%60+is+a+%60DirEntry%60.%0A++++++++++++++++if+let+Ok(metadata)+=+entry.metadata()+%7B%0A++++++++++++++++++++//+Now+let%27s+show+our+entry%27s+permissions!%0A++++++++++++++++++++println!(%22%7B:?%7D:+%7B:?%7D%22,+entry.path(),+metadata.permissions());%0A++++++++++++++++%7D+else+%7B%0A++++++++++++++++++++println!(%22Couldn%27t+get+metadata+for+%7B:?%7D%22,+entry.path());%0A++++++++++++++++%7D%0A++++++++++++%7D%0A++++++++%7D%0A++++%7D%0A%7D&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]},{"type":"anchor","id":"method.file_type"},{"type":"text","value":"1.1.0 · "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/std/fs.rs.html#2562-2564","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source"}]},{"type":"heading","level":4,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"pub fn "},{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/struct.DirEntry.html#method.file_type","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"file_type"}]},{"type":"text","value":"(&self) -> "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/type.Result.html","title":"type std::io::Result","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/struct.FileType.html","title":"struct std::fs::FileType","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FileType"}]},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the file type for the file that this entry points at."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function will not traverse symlinks if this entry points at a symlink."}]},{"type":"heading","level":5,"id":"platform-specific-behavior-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Platform-specific behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On Windows and most Unix platforms this function is free (no extra system calls needed), but some Unix platforms may require the equivalent call to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"symlink_metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" to learn about the target file type."}]},{"type":"heading","level":5,"id":"examples-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"use std::fs;\n\nif let Ok(entries) = fs::read_dir(\".\") {\n    for entry in entries {\n        if let Ok(entry) = entry {\n            // Here, `entry` is a `DirEntry`.\n            if let Ok(file_type) = entry.file_type() {\n                // Now let's show our entry's file type!\n                println!(\"{:?}: {:?}\", entry.path(), file_type);\n            } else {\n                println!(\"Couldn't get file type for {:?}\", entry.path());\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}"},{"ty